   "cumleler": [
    "Two identical signals from the same source behave differently.",
    "If two such signals are in phase, that is, their peaks arrive together, the pressures add and the pressure doubles.",
    "In this case, the level rises by about six decibels, not three.",
    "Two identical signals in opposite phase cancel each other, because the peak of one meets the trough of the other.",
    "Active noise-canceling headphones work on this principle; they reduce mainly low-pitched noise with an opposite-phase signal.",
    "Fully in-phase or fully out-of-phase cases are rare in real settings; for independent sources the three-decibel rule applies."
   ]
