   "cumleler": [
    "In earlier lessons we saw the inverse square law: when distance doubles, intensity drops to one quarter.",
    "A drop to one quarter in intensity means ten times the logarithm of one quarter, or about minus six decibels.",
    "We get the same result from pressure: pressure is halved, and twenty times the logarithm of one half is also about minus six.",
    "The general formula is: the level change is twenty times the logarithm of the ratio of the two distances.",
    "If distance quadruples, the level drops by twelve decibels, and if it rises tenfold, by twenty decibels.",
    "Conversely, halving the distance to the source raises the level by about six decibels.",
    "This calculation applies to a point source in a free field without reflections."
   ]
